* =====================================================================================================
* led_data__nrf52840_gpio.lib -- nRF52840 GPIO push-pull output stage (P0.06 = I2S0 SDOUT = LED_DIN_MCU)
*
* Part      : Nordic nRF52840 (inside the Raytac MDBT50Q module, U10), GPIO in output mode,
*             DRIVE = S0S1 (standard) or H0H1 (high drive), PIN_CNF[n].DRIVE.
* Datasheet : nRF52840 Product Specification 4413_417 v1.1 (2019-02-28),
*             https://cdn.sparkfun.com/assets/d/2/6/2/6/nRF52840_PS_v1.1.pdf (mirror of
*             https://docs.nordicsemi.com/bundle/ps_nrf52840/page/gpio.html), section 6.9.3.1
*             "GPIO Electrical Specification" (p.156-157), Table 172 (recommended operating
*             conditions, p.611) and Table 173 (absolute maximum ratings, p.612).
*             The PS states (section 2) that its electrical tables apply over the recommended operating
*             conditions, i.e. TA = -40 ... +85 C and VDD = 1.7 ... 3.6 V, so the min/max IOH/IOL corners
*             below already contain the temperature spread.
*
* Modelled (all from PS 6.9.3.1):
*   - Pull-up / pull-down as voltage-controlled current sources I = s * ISAT * tanh(Vds / VK), where s is
*     the pre-driver state (0..1). ISAT is set so that I(Vds = 0.4 V) equals the table current exactly:
*       IOH,SD  = 1 / 2 / 4 mA   (min/typ/max) at VOH = VDD - 0.4 V, standard drive, VDD >= 1.7 V
*       IOL,SD  = 1 / 2 / 4 mA   (min/typ/max) at VOL = VSS + 0.4 V
*       IOH,HDH = 6 / 9 / 14 mA  (min/typ/max) at VDD - 0.4 V, high drive, VDD >= 2.7 V
*       IOL,HDH = 6 / 10 / 15 mA (min/typ/max) at VSS + 0.4 V, high drive, VDD >= 2.7 V
*     (so VOH,SD / VOH,HDH >= VDD - 0.4 V at 0.5 mA / 5 mA hold by construction at the min corner).
*     The LED data line loads the pin with only ~35 uA DC (R41 100 k + DI leakage). The PS gives no VOH at that
*     current; a MOSFET's I-V is concave in Vds, so the drop at a small current is at most the chord value
*     0.4 V x I / IOH(min) (13 mV at 33 uA, standard drive). The tanh shape is concave and reproduces that bound.
*   - Shape VK and pre-driver edge TEDGE (10-90 %, first-order) fitted to the PS dynamic table
*     (typical, "based on simulations"), with CPAD = 3 pF (PS CPAD typ) inside the pin:
*       tRF,15/25/50pF  (standard) = 9 / 13 / 25 ns  -> fit VK = 3.0 V, TEDGE = 2.5 ns
*                                                       (model 8.9 / 13.3 / 24.7 ns, 10-90 %, VDD 3.0 V)
*       tHRF,15/25/50pF (high)     = 4 / 5 / 8 ns    -> fit VK = 1.0 V, TEDGE = 4.0 ns
*                                                       (model 3.9 / 5.0 / 7.8 ns)
*     test_led_data.py::test_gpio_model_reproduces_ps_tables re-checks both fits on every run.
*   - Pad ESD clamps to VDD and VSS (generic diode, see NOT modelled).
*
* Parameters: IOH, IOL = table current at 0.4 V drop (A); VK (V); TEDGE (s); CPAD (F).
*   Corner use (in the test): weak = min column, strong = max column, typical = typ column; TEDGE is scaled
*   with the same ratio for weak/strong (conservative assumption: a slow pre-driver goes with a weak driver).
*
* NOT modelled: the real I-V curve beyond the single 0.4 V table point (the tanh shape is a fit to the
*   typical tRF table, not a published curve); output-current-dependent VDD/VSS bounce inside the module;
*   the ESD clamp I-V (PS gives none: generic diode IS=1e-15 A, N=1, RS=5 ohm); the 10-90 % rise/fall times
*   are typical-only in the PS; package/module trace from the die to module pad 22 (a few mm, part of CPAD here).
*
* Pins: out = pad, ctl = ideal logic input (0 V = low, 1 V = high, referenced to gnd), vdd, gnd
*
* Second subckt NRF52840_GPIO_BOUND (added by the independent verifier): the WEAKEST output stage the PS
*   still guarantees. The PS gives only one I-V point per corner (IOH/IOL at a 0.4 V drop) and the tRF/tHRF
*   table is typical-only ("based on simulations"), so the tanh shape above, scaled to the min corner, is an
*   assumption. A MOSFET output's I(Vds) is monotonic and concave, so the guaranteed lower envelope is
*       I >= IOH(min) * min(Vds / 0.4 V, 1)      (and the same for IOL)
*   i.e. a resistor 0.4 V / IOH up to 0.4 V and a constant IOH beyond. Use it with the PS min column
*   (SD 1 mA / HD 6 mA source, 1 mA / 6 mA sink) to get the datasheet-guaranteed edge rates.
*   Pre-driver TEDGE and CPAD as above (they shift both edges alike and hardly matter here).
*
* Third subckt NRF52840_GPIO_HIZ: the pad with the output and input buffer disconnected (PIN_CNF reset
*   value 0x00000002 = input, buffer disconnected, no pull; PS v1.1 6.9.2 PIN_CNF[n]): CPAD and the clamps only.
*   The PS gives no pad leakage figure, so none is modelled (the LED-side leakage dominates the test).
* =====================================================================================================
.subckt NRF52840_GPIO_OUT out ctl vdd gnd params: IOH=2m IOL=2m VK=3.0 TEDGE=2.5n CPAD=3p
.param ISU={IOH/tanh(0.4/VK)} ISD={IOL/tanh(0.4/VK)}
* pre-driver: first-order lag, 10-90 % = TEDGE (= 2.197 tau)
Rpre ctl s 1k
Cpre s gnd {TEDGE/2.1972/1k}
Bup vdd out I = max(min(v(s,gnd),1),0)*ISU*tanh(v(vdd,out)/VK)
Bdn out gnd I = max(min(1-v(s,gnd),1),0)*ISD*tanh(v(out,gnd)/VK)
Cpad out gnd {CPAD}
Desdh out vdd D_NRF_ESD
Desdl gnd out D_NRF_ESD
.model D_NRF_ESD D(IS=1e-15 N=1 RS=5)
.ends NRF52840_GPIO_OUT
* -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* PS-guaranteed lower bound (see the header): I = s * IOH * min(Vds/0.4, 1), reverse conduction allowed.
* VKU / VKD > 0 switch that side to the tanh shape of NRF52840_GPIO_OUT instead (used for the fast side of a
* skew corner, e.g. pull-up at the guaranteed bound and pull-down at the PS max column with the fitted shape).
.subckt NRF52840_GPIO_BOUND out ctl vdd gnd params: IOH=1m IOL=1m VKU=0 VKD=0 TEDGE=2.5n CPAD=3p
.param ISU={VKU > 0 ? IOH/tanh(0.4/max(VKU,1e-3)) : IOH} ISD={VKD > 0 ? IOL/tanh(0.4/max(VKD,1e-3)) : IOL}
.param KU={VKU > 0 ? 1 : 0} KD={VKD > 0 ? 1 : 0} VU={max(VKU,1e-3)} VD={max(VKD,1e-3)}
Rpre ctl s 1k
Cpre s gnd {TEDGE/2.1972/1k}
Bup vdd out I = max(min(v(s,gnd),1),0)*ISU*(KU*tanh(v(vdd,out)/VU) + (1-KU)*max(min(v(vdd,out)/0.4,1),-1))
Bdn out gnd I = max(min(1-v(s,gnd),1),0)*ISD*(KD*tanh(v(out,gnd)/VD) + (1-KD)*max(min(v(out,gnd)/0.4,1),-1))
Cpad out gnd {CPAD}
Desdh out vdd D_NRF_ESD_B
Desdl gnd out D_NRF_ESD_B
.model D_NRF_ESD_B D(IS=1e-15 N=1 RS=5)
.ends NRF52840_GPIO_BOUND
* -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* pad high-Z (reset / DFU / pin not yet configured): CPAD and the clamps only
.subckt NRF52840_GPIO_HIZ out vdd gnd params: CPAD=3p
Cpad out gnd {CPAD}
Desdh out vdd D_NRF_ESD_Z
Desdl gnd out D_NRF_ESD_Z
.model D_NRF_ESD_Z D(IS=1e-15 N=1 RS=5)
.ends NRF52840_GPIO_HIZ
